From 1afec62e7e84210b937e636c78706ba93f13e127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oussama Benjelloun <benje.oussama@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:25:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] HIP: add the HIP runtime (halide_hip_*)

Section-by-section mirror of runtime/cuda.cpp on the HIP API: libamdhip64
is loaded dynamically (no ROCm needed at build time), the device ordinal is
the context, kernels are launched with hipModuleLaunchKernel(kernelParams)
so the HIP runtime packs kernargs from code-object metadata, allocations
use the same free-list reuse as CUDA, and arch detection reads gcnArchName.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
